{{Documentation/Header}}
Renders a full month as a seven-column grid, listing every utaite born on each day. Today's cell is highlighted. Used on [[Birthday Calendar]] and [[Youtaite Wiki:Birthday Calendar]].

Each day cell is produced by {{T|Birthday Calendar/util}}, which runs its own DPL query against <code><nowiki>[[Category:Birthday/MM/DD]]</nowiki></code>. Those categories come from the {{T|Utaite}} infobox — see {{T|ProcessBirthdayCategory}} for the full picture, including the requirement that <code>birthref</code> be filled in.

{{Notice
| header = Performance
| info = One call runs '''up to 31 separate DPL queries''' — one per day. Place it on its own page rather than embedding it in a busy article, and avoid transcluding it more than once per page.
| border = orange
}}

== Syntax ==
{{T|Birthday Calendar|block=1
|v1=month =
|v2=cat =
}}

== Examples ==
<pre>{{Birthday Calendar|month=06}}</pre>
<pre>{{Birthday Calendar|month=02|cat=Youtaite}}</pre>

A live example is not included here because of the query cost — see [[Birthday Calendar]] for the rendered result.

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>month</code> || – || Month || Month to render, '''zero-padded to two digits''' (<code>01</code>–<code>12</code>). If omitted, the header reads "Month" and no days match. || number || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|-
| <code>cat</code> || – || Category filter || Restricts results to pages in a category ending with this text. || string || Utaite ||
|}

== Day handling ==
{| class="dataTable"
! Month !! Days rendered
|-
| February, leap year || 1–29
|-
| February, common year || 1–28
|-
| April, June, September, November || 1–30
|-
| All other months || 1–31
|}

Leap years are detected with <code>{{CURRENTJSTYEAR}} mod 4</code>. This ignores the 100/400-year century rule, which is correct for every year from 1901 to 2099.

== Footer link ==
When the template is used on any page other than [[Birthday Calendar]], it appends a '''"Full calendar here"''' link back to that page.

